<http://data.silknow.org/object/c6288db3-4a42-3885-a60f-b6190d4ead7b>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Tassel of silk, possibly made in France or Italy, 1700-1750"@en , "Tassel of bright yellow silk. The main body is cylindrical (2.5 inches) topped by a smaller bulbous shape (1.5 inches) with a waist. Core of wood covered with silk. The covering consists of strands of bright yellow twisted silk bound flat, and held down by a yellow silk net, simple twisted lattice over the bulbous part and knotted in a chequer pattern over the cylinder. The fringe is made from a portion of the silk covering falls straight with cut ends, 4 inches long. The base is covered by the rest of the yellow silk strands knotted in the hollow centre of the core."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/b257ab9b-0126-343c-8bf5-8cf83158bd3a> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Tassel of silk, possibly made in France or Italy, 1700-1750"@en , "Tassel of bright yellow silk. The main body is cylindrical (2.5 inches) topped by a smaller bulbous shape (1.5 inches) with a waist. Core of wood covered with silk. The covering consists of strands of bright yellow twisted silk bound flat, and held down by a yellow silk net, simple twisted lattice over the bulbous part and knotted in a chequer pattern over the cylinder. The fringe is made from a portion of the silk covering falls straight with cut ends, 4 inches long. The base is covered by the rest of the yellow silk strands knotted in the hollow centre of the core."@en ;
